    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **46 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the change in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`. When a client supplies a `registrationDate`, the controller now rejects it with **400 Bad Request** if it is later than the server's current date:\n\n```java\nOwner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);\nLocalDate suppliedDate = owner.getRegistrationDate();\nif (suppliedDate != null && suppliedDate.isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n}\nLocalDate effectiveDate = suppliedDate != null ? suppliedDate : LocalDate.now();\n```\n\nKey design points:\n- The check runs on the **raw supplied date**, before the business-day roll (`toBusinessDay`), so a valid past/present date isn't accidentally rolled into the future and rejected \u2014 matching the spec's \"supplied registrationDate later than the server date.\"\n- A `null` (unsupplied) registration date still defaults to today, so existing behavior (Cp07, Cp20, Cp21) is unaffected.\n\nThe new checkpoint test `Cp33Tests` (posting `2999-01-01` \u2192 expects 400) passes, and all other existing acceptance tests remain green.",
